1
00:00:00,980 --> 00:00:04,140
Now everybody lift your hands up!

2
00:00:04,260 --> 00:00:06,201
Sing about what you are dreaming!

3
00:00:06,380 --> 00:00:07,740
Always stand up!

4
00:00:07,940 --> 00:00:09,917
Raise up the flag that can't be beaten!

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,420
Gotta keep up!

6
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:15,697
We'll get past every wall that's
in our wake, go without hesitation!

7
00:00:15,780 --> 00:00:16,820
Hands up!

8
00:00:22,860 --> 00:00:26,617
We just have to press on a little more.

9
00:00:26,700 --> 00:00:30,197
To get to the answers we're looking for.

10
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:33,297
We came to this new world believing.

11
00:00:33,380 --> 00:00:37,957
That surely someday we
just might find the way.

12
00:00:38,040 --> 00:00:42,897
All the pieces of our dreams
have now come together.

13
00:00:42,980 --> 00:00:45,357
Our bonds won't waver.

14
00:00:45,440 --> 00:00:47,837
With our dreaming hand.

15
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:49,880
Let's head on towards.

16
00:00:50,660 --> 00:00:52,697
A bright new future.

17
00:00:52,780 --> 00:00:56,537
Now everybody lift your hands up.

18
00:00:56,620 --> 00:00:58,597
Sing about what you are dreaming.

19
00:00:58,680 --> 00:01:00,237
Always stand up.

20
00:01:00,320 --> 00:01:02,397
Raise up the flag that you believe in.

21
00:01:02,480 --> 00:01:03,957
Gotta keep up.

22
00:01:04,040 --> 00:01:06,317
We'll get past everyone that's in our way.

23
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:08,400
Let's head on never stopping.

24
00:01:09,660 --> 00:01:11,337
Only look up.

25
00:01:11,420 --> 00:01:13,337
Keep your head up way up high.

26
00:01:13,420 --> 00:01:15,037
Always step up.

27
00:01:15,120 --> 00:01:17,017
If waves are rough, jump to the sky.

28
00:01:17,100 --> 00:01:18,797
Never give up.

29
00:01:18,880 --> 00:01:20,777
Our wishes, they will come together.

30
00:01:20,860 --> 00:01:23,200
And lead us on for the future.

31
00:01:24,680 --> 00:01:27,837
We drift on riding the waves.

32
00:01:27,920 --> 00:01:30,717
Towards another shore day by day.

33
00:01:30,800 --> 00:01:35,497
There are many meetings, many goodbyes.

34
00:01:35,580 --> 00:01:37,820
Underneath the flag we fly.

35
00:01:41,060 --> 00:01:43,697
I'll remember the pain within.

36
00:01:43,780 --> 00:01:45,857
I'll keep it in my heart forever.

37
00:01:45,940 --> 00:01:47,977
And never take it lightly.

38
00:01:48,060 --> 00:01:49,837
But I won't surrender.

39
00:01:49,920 --> 00:01:52,037
This freedom I will keep in mind.

40
00:01:52,120 --> 00:01:54,617
I'll keep holding on, never stop it.

41
00:01:54,700 --> 00:01:57,437
Now everybody lift your hands up.

42
00:01:57,520 --> 00:01:59,517
Sing about what you are dreaming.

43
00:01:59,600 --> 00:02:01,157
Always stand up.

44
00:02:01,240 --> 00:02:03,337
Raise up the flag that you believe in.

45
00:02:03,420 --> 00:02:04,897
Gotta keep up.

46
00:02:04,980 --> 00:02:07,237
We'll get past everyone that's in our way.

47
00:02:07,320 --> 00:02:09,760
Let's head on, never stop it.

48
00:02:10,880 --> 00:02:14,337
Only look up, keep your
head up way up high.

49
00:02:14,420 --> 00:02:17,957
Always step up, if brains
are rough, jump to the sky.

50
00:02:18,040 --> 00:02:21,637
Never give up, our wishes,
they will come together.

51
00:02:21,720 --> 00:02:24,160
And lead us on for the future.

52
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:26,120
Hands up.

53
00:02:30,440 --> 00:02:33,857
Uh, Luffy, take a good
long look at this lake.

54
00:02:33,940 --> 00:02:35,940
Are you sure you want to cross it?

55
00:02:36,180 --> 00:02:38,300
Uh-huh You gotta be kidding me!

56
00:02:38,660 --> 00:02:40,857
It's going to be impossible
to get across that thing!

57
00:02:40,940 --> 00:02:43,293
Half's on fire, the other half's frozen!

58
00:02:43,480 --> 00:02:46,680
Then the temperature of the
water should be perfect.

59
00:02:47,280 --> 00:02:48,880
Let's swim. You're crazy!

60
00:02:49,120 --> 00:02:52,061
Robin and I can't get wet,
so you know what to do.

61
00:02:55,520 --> 00:02:58,814
Are you trying to imply that
we should carry you across?

62
00:03:00,020 --> 00:03:03,177
Actually, if we don't cross, we'll
have to go all the way around.

63
00:03:03,260 --> 00:03:04,517
I've got no choice.

64
00:03:04,600 --> 00:03:07,920
In that case, let me see what I can do.

65
00:03:09,120 --> 00:03:11,000
Special attack, Green Star!

66
00:03:12,820 --> 00:03:14,020
Grow, Fangrass!

67
00:03:15,600 --> 00:03:17,380
Never seen this plant before.

68
00:03:17,640 --> 00:03:18,600
Booty banana!

69
00:03:22,780 --> 00:03:24,200
What? A boot!

70
00:03:24,440 --> 00:03:25,980
This is awesome, Usopp!

71
00:03:26,220 --> 00:03:28,500
We can use this Fangrass's oars.

72
00:03:29,320 --> 00:03:31,614
You've got so many different seeds now.

73
00:03:31,720 --> 00:03:32,557
How nice.

74
00:03:32,640 --> 00:03:34,780
They're pretty handy, aren't they?

75
00:03:35,160 --> 00:03:37,817
There were a bunch of crazy
plants in the Bowen Islands.

76
00:03:37,900 --> 00:03:40,277
The deeper I went into
the dangerous areas,

77
00:03:40,360 --> 00:03:43,037
the more useful the plants
I found along the way.

78
00:03:43,120 --> 00:03:45,296
I survived there for two whole years.

79
00:03:45,380 --> 00:03:48,780
There's no difficulty I
can't overcome! Nope! Not me!

80
00:03:49,220 --> 00:03:50,620
Grandpa, get on board!

81
00:03:50,740 --> 00:03:52,200
Or we'll leave you! Hey!

82
00:03:52,680 --> 00:03:54,977
Just don't forget who supplied the boat!

83
00:03:55,060 --> 00:03:56,160
All right, guys!

84
00:03:56,520 --> 00:03:57,900
Let's take that away!

85
00:03:58,780 --> 00:04:00,240
I want snow cones!

86
00:04:00,560 --> 00:04:01,854
Why aren't you rowing?

87
00:04:03,860 --> 00:04:04,690
Wow!

88
00:04:04,800 --> 00:04:05,660
So breezy!

89
00:04:05,860 --> 00:04:07,037
There's a strong headwind.

90
00:04:07,120 --> 00:04:07,950
Of course.

91
00:04:08,033 --> 00:04:09,977
It's the temperature difference here.

92
00:04:10,060 --> 00:04:13,300
It creates a change in air
pressure, causing wind.

93
00:04:13,540 --> 00:04:14,937
Look, the water's boiling.

94
00:04:15,020 --> 00:04:18,797
You see, if we tried to swim across,
we'd have been poached pirates.

95
00:04:18,880 --> 00:04:20,351
Can't you row any faster?

96
00:04:20,580 --> 00:04:22,815
Why don't you try helping us, you bum?

97
00:04:22,940 --> 00:04:24,880
You're not getting away.

98
00:04:25,820 --> 00:04:27,060
Come back here!

99
00:04:27,780 --> 00:04:28,740
Oh, crap!

100
00:04:29,940 --> 00:04:32,220
Not that centaur again! Hey!

101
00:04:32,640 --> 00:04:35,897
Let me guess, you changed your
mind and decided to join us?

102
00:04:35,980 --> 00:04:38,097
Would you quit recruiting folks, Luffy?

103
00:04:38,180 --> 00:04:42,415
Yeah, it's not like we need any more
strange creatures joining the crew.

104
00:04:45,240 --> 00:04:46,260
A horn?

105
00:04:47,360 --> 00:04:48,560
No, boss!

106
00:04:49,140 --> 00:04:49,970
Boss?

107
00:04:50,140 --> 00:04:51,377
That guy on the snail.

108
00:04:51,460 --> 00:04:53,578
He said something about a boss, too.

109
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:55,520
Please, it's cold.

110
00:04:55,840 --> 00:04:57,320
We need boss.

111
00:04:57,720 --> 00:04:59,520
Finish off the intruders.

112
00:04:59,840 --> 00:05:01,700
They're headed right for you.

113
00:05:05,340 --> 00:05:07,197
Look at the shore on the other side.

114
00:05:07,280 --> 00:05:08,117
Someone's there.

115
00:05:08,200 --> 00:05:09,030
Where?

116
00:05:17,540 --> 00:05:19,760
Guess that's the boss.

117
00:05:20,140 --> 00:05:22,177
The distress signal was meant for him?

118
00:05:22,260 --> 00:05:24,997
If that's the case, we don't
have anything to worry about.

119
00:05:25,080 --> 00:05:29,315
This boss guy's got bigger problems
to deal with than us washing ashore.

120
00:05:32,660 --> 00:05:35,960
There's a man among them
who's carrying swords.

121
00:05:36,220 --> 00:05:38,720
Is he the samurai who attacked our people?

122
00:05:39,440 --> 00:05:42,800
If so, I'll make him pay.

123
00:05:47,260 --> 00:05:49,731
There's something creepy about this place.

124
00:05:49,920 --> 00:05:53,155
It feels like we're being
watched by Akainu and Aokiji.

125
00:05:53,700 --> 00:05:55,520
The thought gives me chills.

126
00:05:55,880 --> 00:05:58,240
We should go back. Fire!

127
00:06:13,620 --> 00:06:14,560
It's a river!

128
00:06:15,880 --> 00:06:18,180
Way to go, Smokey! That was amazing!

129
00:06:18,360 --> 00:06:19,478
I can't believe it!

130
00:06:19,600 --> 00:06:22,477
How'd you know there was a
river behind that block of ice?

131
00:06:22,560 --> 00:06:24,660
That was pretty impressive, Smokey!

132
00:06:24,800 --> 00:06:27,388
It's like you got Saru
vision or something!

133
00:06:32,640 --> 00:06:35,757
You can tell by looking at
the sea current, you morons.

134
00:06:35,840 --> 00:06:38,277
You men need to start paying attention and

135
00:06:38,360 --> 00:06:40,657
work on your attitudes while you're at it.

136
00:06:40,740 --> 00:06:42,160
It is worrisome, sir.

137
00:06:43,180 --> 00:06:44,700
That it is. Huh?

138
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:49,706
The fact that there was a hidden
river is not what's important.

139
00:06:49,860 --> 00:06:51,160
In this situation,

140
00:06:51,440 --> 00:06:56,600
what really matters is whether the ice
blocking it formed naturally or was man-made.

141
00:06:57,160 --> 00:06:58,240
Hold up, Smokey.

142
00:06:58,480 --> 00:07:02,277
You mean somebody might have been
hiding the river from us on purpose?

143
00:07:02,360 --> 00:07:03,948
Come on, nobody lives here.

144
00:07:04,100 --> 00:07:05,688
It's full of poisonous gas.

145
00:07:05,800 --> 00:07:09,477
They'd have to be crazy to want to
live out their days in a gas mask.

146
00:07:09,560 --> 00:07:13,077
The man on the snail definitely
mentioned the name of this island.

147
00:07:13,160 --> 00:07:15,437
You probably just misheard him, Tashigi.

148
00:07:15,520 --> 00:07:18,344
Not even a transponder
snail could survive here.

149
00:07:19,620 --> 00:07:20,900
He's got a point.

150
00:07:23,020 --> 00:07:26,902
If you've got time to laugh, you've
got time to break up more ice.

151
00:07:31,680 --> 00:07:33,077
What in the hell is that?

152
00:07:33,160 --> 00:07:35,440
Holy crap, it's a giant wall of ice!

153
00:07:35,840 --> 00:07:39,337
Her warship is strong, but it's
no match for something that size.

154
00:07:39,420 --> 00:07:40,300
What'll we do?

155
00:07:40,480 --> 00:07:42,800
We've got to destroy it! Fire!

156
00:07:54,220 --> 00:07:55,180
Wah-choo!

157
00:07:57,360 --> 00:07:59,184
Okay, time to bust out of here!

158
00:07:59,380 --> 00:08:00,477
Are you with me?

159
00:08:00,560 --> 00:08:01,500
Let's go!

160
00:08:01,780 --> 00:08:03,577
You're really fired up,
aren't you, Chopper?

161
00:08:03,660 --> 00:08:04,490
You know it.

162
00:08:04,573 --> 00:08:06,497
Sanji trusted me with
an important mission.

163
00:08:06,580 --> 00:08:09,137
That means I gotta do my
best to protect the children.

164
00:08:09,220 --> 00:08:11,697
I'll do whatever it takes
to get the job done.

165
00:08:11,780 --> 00:08:12,960
Just watch me.

166
00:08:13,460 --> 00:08:16,517
I'll get you out of here if
it's the last thing I do!

167
00:08:16,600 --> 00:08:17,480
Watch out!

168
00:08:25,420 --> 00:08:26,714
Don't be scared, kids.

169
00:08:26,820 --> 00:08:30,080
I laugh in the face of
danger, because I'm a man!

170
00:08:30,560 --> 00:08:32,657
Where do you think we should go from here?

171
00:08:32,740 --> 00:08:33,799
I'm just security.

172
00:08:33,940 --> 00:08:35,705
That's up to you, little lady.

173
00:08:36,100 --> 00:08:36,930
Huh?

174
00:08:37,200 --> 00:08:39,520
Miss, are you sure I'll be okay?

175
00:08:40,360 --> 00:08:41,520
Oh, I'm positive.

176
00:08:41,960 --> 00:08:43,237
You don't have to worry.

177
00:08:43,320 --> 00:08:45,817
We're experts at getting
out of dangerous situations.

178
00:08:45,900 --> 00:08:47,620
Just relax and follow us.

179
00:08:51,700 --> 00:08:52,700
Watch out!

180
00:09:03,420 --> 00:09:04,980
Now you made me mad!

181
00:09:05,580 --> 00:09:06,540
Weapons, live!

182
00:09:14,380 --> 00:09:15,210
Super!

183
00:09:17,060 --> 00:09:19,119
He's got weapons all over his body.

184
00:09:19,240 --> 00:09:22,560
Yeah, he must be the one who
broke the door open. Huh?

185
00:09:23,160 --> 00:09:26,160
Sounds like you guys want
to get to know me better.

186
00:09:26,540 --> 00:09:29,517
Okay, I'll spend as much
time here as you want, bro!

187
00:09:29,600 --> 00:09:31,337
Load the poison gas canisters!

188
00:09:31,420 --> 00:09:33,655
The kits are gone, the coast is clear!

189
00:09:34,060 --> 00:09:35,740
All right, fire at will!

190
00:09:42,200 --> 00:09:44,671
You should take off your masks, gentlemen.

191
00:09:44,780 --> 00:09:47,137
Don't you want to smoke
poisonous gas with us?

192
00:09:47,220 --> 00:09:48,050
Bastard!

193
00:09:48,133 --> 00:09:50,311
Calm down, there's no reason to get angry.

194
00:10:00,480 --> 00:10:02,137
He rips our masks off!

195
00:10:02,220 --> 00:10:03,717
And he broke our air tanks!

196
00:10:03,800 --> 00:10:05,300
Don't use gas canisters!

197
00:10:07,340 --> 00:10:09,860
Whoa, what in the hell are you? Sheep?

198
00:10:14,720 --> 00:10:15,600
Why you?

199
00:10:16,740 --> 00:10:18,477
Just what are you doing down there?

200
00:10:18,560 --> 00:10:19,957
Who on earth could this be?

201
00:10:20,040 --> 00:10:22,417
This foe is different from
the others I've fought.

202
00:10:22,500 --> 00:10:24,217
I've never been challenged like this.

203
00:10:24,300 --> 00:10:26,700
They're quite the formidable opponent.

204
00:10:26,980 --> 00:10:29,277
I got no clue what you're
talking about, bro.

205
00:10:29,360 --> 00:10:30,190
Sorry.

206
00:10:30,273 --> 00:10:32,200
My torso's currently in battle.

207
00:10:32,840 --> 00:10:33,670
Say what?

208
00:10:42,980 --> 00:10:44,117
What's going on?

209
00:10:44,200 --> 00:10:45,141
I'm so confused.

210
00:10:45,980 --> 00:10:48,980
Who are you and why are
you attacking me like this?

211
00:10:50,600 --> 00:10:51,900
Where'd your head go?

212
00:10:52,180 --> 00:10:53,592
And where are your legs?

213
00:10:57,400 --> 00:10:58,840
How fretful!

214
00:10:59,080 --> 00:11:00,845
I don't suppose you can speak.

215
00:11:07,240 --> 00:11:08,820
Ready? Fire!

216
00:11:29,820 --> 00:11:32,585
We're going to reach the
end of the river soon.

217
00:11:34,120 --> 00:11:34,950
Really?

218
00:11:35,033 --> 00:11:36,684
I wonder what we'll find there.

219
00:11:37,800 --> 00:11:39,840
I've got a pretty good idea.

220
00:11:48,180 --> 00:11:51,592
You wouldn't happen to be a
ghost bike, Chance, would you?

221
00:11:51,840 --> 00:11:53,940
If so, you need to obey the rules.

222
00:11:54,720 --> 00:11:56,617
You can't come out during the day?

223
00:11:56,700 --> 00:11:58,457
Why are you attacking me?

224
00:11:58,540 --> 00:11:59,957
I didn't do anything wrong.

225
00:12:00,040 --> 00:12:03,177
The only reason I came ashore
was to make a snow army.

226
00:12:03,260 --> 00:12:05,097
There's no point in fighting.

227
00:12:05,180 --> 00:12:06,637
Why don't we build snowmen instead?

228
00:12:06,720 --> 00:12:09,400
We can make snow sculptures if you like.

229
00:12:16,100 --> 00:12:20,017
I don't understand how
he can attack with such

230
00:12:20,100 --> 00:12:22,377
precision when he doesn't
even have any eyes?

231
00:12:22,460 --> 00:12:26,957
No wait a minute!

232
00:12:27,040 --> 00:12:28,137
I just remembered!

233
00:12:28,220 --> 00:12:29,926
I don't have any eyes either.

234
00:12:38,860 --> 00:12:41,297
He's strong! And... Stay

235
00:12:41,380 --> 00:12:48,380
back!

236
00:12:52,120 --> 00:12:53,637
I demand answers from you!

237
00:12:53,720 --> 00:12:56,602
Can't you at least tell
me why you wish to fight?

238
00:12:57,080 --> 00:12:58,317
You asked for it.

239
00:12:58,400 --> 00:12:59,780
Hop-up-cour-droit!

240
00:13:06,320 --> 00:13:07,820
Two-sword style?

241
00:13:09,380 --> 00:13:11,909
Okay, now he's really
starting to scare me!

242
00:13:12,300 --> 00:13:14,520
I can't handle it! He's so creepy!

243
00:13:14,860 --> 00:13:16,440
And now somebody save me!

244
00:13:32,140 --> 00:13:36,137
You called master yes did you capture the

245
00:13:36,220 --> 00:13:40,140
escapees not yet but i
have news about g5 sir

246
00:13:40,980 --> 00:13:44,940
Oh them i'm afraid the
poison gas didn't stop them

247
00:13:47,900 --> 00:13:49,997
They've been firing their
cannons to break through the

248
00:13:50,080 --> 00:13:53,492
ice flows They're slowly forcing
their way onto the island

249
00:13:54,660 --> 00:14:00,297
It looks like they'll make their
way to the laboratory soon this is

250
00:14:00,380 --> 00:14:05,957
quite vexing why do They want to
come ashore so badly do they know

251
00:14:06,040 --> 00:14:11,477
something we don't tell me who is
their commanding Officer vice admiral

252
00:14:11,560 --> 00:14:17,617
smoker oh is that so irksome but

253
00:14:17,700 --> 00:14:19,880
not entirely unexpected i suppose

254
00:14:21,220 --> 00:14:22,161
All right, then.

255
00:14:22,560 --> 00:14:24,717
Conceal the ships we
have moored at the front.

256
00:14:24,800 --> 00:14:26,617
Who's going to deal with them, sir?

257
00:14:26,700 --> 00:14:28,994
No one is allowed to be on this island.

258
00:14:29,740 --> 00:14:32,100
That means you cannot let them see you.

259
00:14:32,540 --> 00:14:34,011
So you'll deal with them?

260
00:14:34,200 --> 00:14:35,420
Don't be a fool.

261
00:14:35,760 --> 00:14:38,113
I can't afford to reveal myself to them.

262
00:14:38,300 --> 00:14:39,217
Then what do we do?

263
00:14:39,300 --> 00:14:41,535
There's nobody else who can stop them.

264
00:14:42,420 --> 00:14:44,700
You want me to handle it? Huh?

